{
	title: 'Pin the CLI contract',
	spec: "Scripts, agents and diffs rely on this exact 0.3.0 behavior. Structured output: records list fields in the order id, title, spec, status, once, notes, needs, foldInto; show adds needs as [{ id, title, status }] and then neededBy, foldedBy and files (all always present, possibly empty); tree emits { nodes, dependencies: [{ from, to }], foldInto: [{ from, to }] }; del emits { id, deleted: true }; init emits { tasksDir }; empty lists print []. Task files: new ones are written in the same field order without id; two or more notes are written one per line; edits preserve comments. Human output: a row is 'STATUS task <id>: <title> (<counts>): <spec excerpt> (<size>)', where counts are once, needs <ids>, N notes, N files (omitting empty ones) and only the excerpt is shortened with … to keep the row within 80 columns; ls ends with 'N planned tasks found, M done.'; add prints the new row, del prints its row with DELETED; show prints the header line, the spec indented two spaces, then only nonempty sections such as '  notes:' with '    - ' items; tree draws needs with ├── └── │ and marks a task reached again as '<id> (also needs <other>; shown above)', with fold targets as '    foldInto → a, b'; reset prints 'Reset N tasks to planned.' plus ' M tasks left done (once).' when any are; an empty result prints 'No results.'. CLI: tsk --version and tsk version print 'tsk X.Y.Z'; tsk, -h and --help print the same summary listing every command; every command accepts --help with Usage, Example and Options sections; init accepts --format; add --status done skips prerequisite checks; repeated --needs and --fold-into are deduplicated; edit --once false writes once: false; add-note takes its text verbatim even when it looks like an option; a value option followed by another --option is missing its value ('--x requires a value'); a repeated --format is an error. Errors are 'tsk: ' plus a lowercase message on stderr with exit 1 and no stdout; failing writes leave files unchanged. del refuses tasks that other tasks need or fold into, even with --force, which only permits deleting the task's files. Tests are rebuilt with the code and check only behavior through the CLI.",
